; The four-fives 84 (Winning 42, p. 113): fives are trump and the bidder holds
; 5-5 5-4 5-2 5-0 4-4 4-2 2-2. The book's first way to be set: an opponent
; holds the six-five together with another five, so it can follow the first
; trump lead and win a trick with the six-five later.
(query
  (roles (chair bidder) (chair foe) (domino other))
  (out)
  (pattern
    (viewer bidder)
    (opponent bidder foe)
    (holds foe 6-5)
    (holds foe other)
    (in other q*)
    (not (tile other 6-5))))
